    AI Technology
    AI Technology means any and all AI Models, AI technology, tools, systems, platforms, methods, works of authorship, designs, inventions, discoveries, trade secrets, know-how, processes, specifications, documentation, code (including source code and object code), algorithms, training datasets (excluding Customer Content), architectures, Model Weights and pre-trained weights, model parameters, and any other tangible or intangible assets or Intellectual Property Rights provided by Provider in connection with this Agreement
    
    *****
    
    Do No Harm Principles
    Do No Harm Principles refer to a commitment by each Party to (i) develop, use and deploy the AI Technology, including any associated data, outputs (such as Customer Content) or derivatives, in a manner that [(a) does not knowingly cause or facilitate direct, indirect, or unintended harm to individuals, communities, the environment, or society; ][(b) respects internationally recognized ethical, humanitarian and human rights standards; and (c)] prohibits any dual-use or military application of the technology in contravention of applicable law or principles of responsible innovation (including, without limitation, the OECD AI Principles and guidelines and policies issued by the International Committee of the Red Cross); and (ii) ensure that no portion of the AI Technology or related deliverables is weaponized, repurposed, or otherwise exploited in a manner inconsistent with such OECD AI Principles.
    
